## 1. Grant of Individual Rights (Sovereign Use)

Subject to the restrictions outlined in Section 2, the Steward hereby grants You - as a sovereign Individual - a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive license to use, reproduce, modify, and deploy the Software for your personal, educational, and individual commercial benefit.

- **Commercial Application:** As an Individual, you are expressly permitted to construct commercial applications, services, or products on top of the Software and derive infinite profit from such creations.
- **Freedom of Modification:** You maintain the absolute right to read, branch, modify, and contribute back to this codebase, preserving the inherent transparency of the Software.

## 2. Restrictions & The Viral Commons

To preserve the integrity of the protocol layer and ensure that the ecosystem thrives symmetrically, the rights granted in Section 1 are explicitly conditioned upon your strict adherence to the following restrictions.

- **No Protocol Resale:** You shall not host, white-label, rebrand, or distribute the Software - or any derivative work retaining substantial architectural similarity to it - as a standalone commercial Platform-as-a-Service (PaaS) or Software-as-a-Service (SaaS). This restriction solely targets the repackaging and resale of the core engine and shall not restrict the distribution of distinct products or interfaces built to run _upon_ the framework.
- **The Tollbridge Prohibition:** While you are permitted to monetize custom experiences built _on top_ of the Software, you shall not erect explicit monetary gates, rent-seeking smart contracts, or proprietary lock-ins that restrict public access to the underlying protocol layer itself.
- **The Symmetric Commons Clause (Copyleft):** If you modify the core architectural components of the Software (the engine) and deploy those modifications for public or commercial use, you must make the complete source code of your modifications publicly available under the exact terms of this Covenant. You may not hoard structural improvements. All tides must rise together.
- **The Synthetic Replication Clause:** You shall not utilize the Software, its source code, its documentation, or its architectural patterns to train, fine-tune, or prompt an Artificial Intelligence model for the purpose of generating a competing framework, bypassing the restrictions of this Covenant, or executing a "clean-room" recreation of the Software.

## 3. Institutional Licensing (Organizational & Enterprise Use)

Any utilization of the Software by, or on behalf of, an Organization operating at scale requires an **Institutional License** obtained exclusively and directly from the Steward, irrespective of whether the Organization designates itself as for-profit, non-profit, or educational.

- **The Grassroots Exception:** Organizations operating entirely below the Enterprise Thresholds (as defined below) may utilize the Software without an Institutional License.
- **The Enterprise Thresholds:** An Institutional License is unconditionally required if the operating Organization, or its parent entity, meets any of the following criteria:
  - It operates as a publicly-traded corporation, government agency, or university.
  - It maintains a dedicated global headcount exceeding 50 employees or independent contractors.
  - It processes or serves in excess of 50,000 monthly active users within an enclosed platform.

- **Exclusive Licensing Authority:** The Steward (including any designated successor or Decentralized Autonomous Organization) retains sole and absolute authority to issue, revoke, or modify Institutional Licenses. The Steward reserves the right to establish the terms of such licenses, including educational exemptions or enterprise fees, at its sole discretion. No third party may sublicense or broker access to the Software for organizational use.
- **Licensing Instrument:** The Steward reserves the right to denominate Institutional Licenses in any financial instrument it deems appropriate, including fiat currency, native digital tokens, cryptocurrencies, or any successor economic mechanism, to sustain the sovereign ecosystem surrounding the Software.

## 4. Attribution & Redistribution

Any redistribution of the Software, whether in its original or modified form, must satisfy the following conditions:

- The complete, unmodified text of this True Omni-Source License must be included.
- The original copyright notice of the Licensor must be preserved intact.
- Any modifications from the original work must be clearly distinguished to prevent misrepresentation of the Software's origins.

Failure to comply with these conditions results in the automatic and immediate termination of all rights granted under Section 1.

## 5. The Steward's Rights (Licensor Sovereignty)

The Steward remains the sole and exclusive copyright holder of the Software. Nothing in this Covenant shall be construed as restricting the Steward from exercising its full intellectual property rights. The Steward may issue independent licensing agreements, forge enterprise partnerships, and deploy the Software in any proprietary manner it deems necessary. The Steward is wholly unbound by the restrictions placed upon the public or licensees by this Covenant.

## 6. Contributions & Intellectual Sovereignty

By submitting a contribution (including, but not limited to, a pull request, patch, or code submission) to the Software, the contributor irrevocably grants the Steward a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive, perpetual license to use, modify, sublicense, and distribute the contribution under the terms of this Covenant or any other license the Steward deems appropriate. The contributor warrants that they possess the legal right to grant this license. The contributor retains the right to utilize their own contribution for any independent purpose.

## 7. Termination & Cure

- **Automatic Termination:** All rights granted under this Covenant terminate automatically upon any violation of Section 2 or any commercial operation lacking a valid license pursuant to Section 3.
- **Cure Period:** If the violating party has not previously breached this Covenant, their rights shall be automatically reinstated provided the violation is completely cured within thirty (30) days of discovery. This grace period provides protection for good-faith actors experiencing accidental non-compliance.
- **No Cure for Bad Faith:** If a violation is willful, repeated, or constitutes a deliberate attempt to circumvent the protections established herein, no cure period shall be granted, and termination shall be immediate and permanent.

## 8. Immutability & The Dead Man's Switch (The Commons Protocol)

To permanently defend the long-term vision against institutional decay, hostile corporate acquisition, or a future steward abandoning the core purpose, this Covenant mandates an irrevocable fail-safe mechanism:

- **Irrevocability of Prior Code:** The permissions granted in Section 1 are legally irrevocable for any iteration of the codebase released under this Covenant.
- **The Trigger:** In the event that the Steward is acquired by a publicly-traded corporation, OR the Steward's executive leadership attempts to retroactively revoke this Covenant to close-source extant versions of the repository, the Dead Man's Switch is immediately and automatically triggered.
- **The Protocol Fallback:** Upon triggering, the license governing all extant versions of the Software covered by this Covenant shall permanently convert to the **GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 (AGPLv3)**.
- **Good-Faith Licensee Protection:** To prevent disruption to the ecosystem, any valid Institutional License legitimately issued by the Steward prior to the triggering of the Dead Man's Switch shall remain in full force and effect under its original terms until its natural expiration.
- **Standing to Invoke:** Any past or present contributor to the codebase, any licensee currently operating under this Covenant, or any designated trustee appointed by the Steward possesses legal standing to publicly declare the Dead Man's Switch triggered and to mandate the AGPLv3 conversion in any court of competent jurisdiction. The burden of proof demonstrating that the Covenant has NOT been violated shall rest entirely with the Steward or its successor entity.

## 9. The 42-Month Release (The Change Date)

To guarantee that the foundational technology of YouMeOS ultimately belongs to the global commons, this Covenant incorporates a rolling release mechanism inspired by the Business Source License (BSL).

- **The Rolling Conversion:** Exactly forty-two (42) months following the initial public release of any specific version of the Software under this Covenant (the "Change Date"), all restrictions imposed by Section 2 and all Institutional Licensing requirements imposed by Section 3 shall automatically and irrevocably dissolve for that specific version.
- **The AGPLv3 Fallback:** Upon reaching its Change Date, that specific version of the Software shall automatically transition to, and be permanently governed by, the **GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 (AGPLv3)**. The AGPLv3 explicitly requires anyone running modified versions in the cloud to contribute their code back to the commons.
- **Scope of Conversion:** This rolling 42-month Change Date applies strictly to the specific, historical version of the codebase reaching its maturity. It does not affect newer, actively maintained versions of the Software, which remain protected under this Covenant until their respective Change Dates.

## 10. Modular Licensing

The Steward retains the authority to designate specific modules, plugins, or sub-components of the project to be governed by separate open-source licenses (e.g., GPLv3, AGPLv3, MIT) to facilitate broader community interoperability. Such designations shall not compromise or alter the protections of this Covenant over the core Software.

## 11. License Versioning & The Immutable Core

The Steward reserves the right to publish new, revised, or updated versions of this Covenant iteratively (e.g., Version 2.0) to address unforeseen legal, technological, or planetary realities.

- **The Immutable Core:** No future version of this Covenant may ever revoke the fundamental rights of Sovereign Use (Section 1), the Institutional Licensing authority (Section 3), the Dead Man's Switch mechanism (Section 8), or the 42-Month Release (Section 9). Any published update attempting to abrogate these protections is fundamentally void _ab initio_ and cannot be applied to any iteration of the Software.
- **Opt-In Adherence:** You may choose to operate under the exact terms of the version under which the Software was originally distributed to you, or you may opt to adhere to any subsequent valid version published by the Steward.

## 12. Governing Law & Jurisdiction (The Planetary Clause)

This Covenant is architected to endure beyond the lifespan of any extant nation-state or localized legal system. Accordingly:

- **Primary Jurisdiction:** This Covenant shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the sovereign jurisdiction in which the Steward (or its legal successor) is domiciled at the time a dispute arises.
- **Concurrent Jurisdiction:** The Steward may additionally bring enforcement actions in the jurisdiction where the alleged violator is domiciled or primarily operates, invoking that jurisdiction's applicable intellectual property and contract laws.
- **International Cooperation:** In matters involving multi-jurisdictional parties, this Covenant explicitly invokes applicable international intellectual property treaties, including but not limited to the Berne Convention for the Protection of Literary and Artistic Works and the WIPO Copyright Treaty. All signatory nations to these treaties are expected to uphold the IP protections established herein.
- **Severability:** Should any provision of this Covenant be held unenforceable under the laws of a particular jurisdiction, the remaining provisions shall remain in full force and effect. The unenforceable provision shall be legally reformed to the minimum extent necessary to render it enforceable while fiercely preserving its original philosophical and economic intent.

## 13. Public Adoption (Using this Covenant for Your Code)

The text of this document itself is dedicated to the public domain. Any creator, sovereign individual, or organization is enthusiastically encouraged to adopt, modify, or apply this Covenant to protect their own visionary architecture.

